      "description": "Mobile discovery cue and keyboard-accessible wide table.",
      "html": "<p class=\"ds-scroll-hint\">Scroll horizontally to see all stage indicators.</p><div class=\"ds-table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Scrollable evidence table\"><table class=\"ds-table\"><thead><tr><th>Crop stage</th><th>Dates</th><th>Heat days</th><th>Rain ≥20 mm days</th><th>Longest dry spell</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Vegetative</th><td>2024-06-01<br><small>to 2024-07-25</small></td><td>0</td><td>5</td><td>2 days</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
      "css": ".ds-scroll-hint{font-family:\"IBM Plex Sans\",sans-serif;display:none;color:var(--muted,#59665f);font-size:12px;margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6}.ds-table-wrap{max-width:100%;overflow:auto;scrollbar-color:#aab8af var(--raised,#f6f8f7);scrollbar-width:thin}.ds-table-wrap:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#126a82)}.ds-table{font-family:\"IBM Plex Sans\",sans-serif;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--ink,#18221e)}.ds-table th,.ds-table td{padding:11px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #edf1ee;text-align:right;vertical-align:middle}.ds-table th:first-child,.ds-table td:first-child{text-align:left;padding-left:0}.ds-table th:last-child,.ds-table td:last-child{padding-right:0}.ds-table thead th{font-size:11px;font-weight:400;color:var(--muted,#59665f);line-height:1.5}.ds-table tbody th{font-weight:400}.ds-table small{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted,#59665f)}@media(max-width:680px){.ds-scroll-hint{display:block}.ds-table{min-width:470px}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Field Planning Sheet",
    "overview": "A green-grey workspace frames a white working sheet. Quiet ink, restrained teal marks and compact IBM Plex Sans typography keep the interface practical for farmers and extension advisers working through historical evidence.\n\nThe recurring visual signature is a pair of crop calendars with proportional stage strips, followed by shared-year comparisons. Color identifies plans and stages; labels, units and tables carry the meaning. The visual system keeps historical exposure and independent economic assumptions legible without presenting either as a validated crop prediction.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Green-grey frame and white working sheet.",
      "Flat, softly rounded groups with fine separators.",
      "Compact labels, tabular numbers and explicit units.",
      "Teal climate marks paired with muted comparison colors.",
      "Responsive stacking with discoverable, keyboard-accessible evidence tables."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Evidence Label Rule",
        "body": "Keep plan names, stage labels and units alongside color; color alone does not explain a result.",
        "section": "colors"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve the green-grey frame, white sheet and flat pale panels.",
      "Do use self-hosted IBM Plex Sans and tabular numbers for the working interface.",
      "Do retain plan names, units and exact-value tables alongside chart colors.",
      "Do keep keyboard focus visible and scrollable evidence regions named and focusable.",
      "Do retain the mobile horizontal-scroll cue beside the stage evidence table.",
      "Do keep source limits and the distinction between exposure and economics visible."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add shadows or decorative gradients to the existing panel hierarchy.",
      "Don't encode a winning plan or predicted crop damage through the comparison palette.",
      "Don't shrink wide evidence tables until their units and dates become unreadable.",
      "Don't replace visible field labels with placeholder-only controls.",
      "Don't add motion that ignores the existing reduced-motion preference."
    ]
  }
